PHASE 29A — Media Buyer Contract, Terms Acceptance, and Commission Agreement

Goal:
Add a contract/terms acceptance flow for Media Buyers before they can access their dashboard.

Important:
This is not legal advice. The contract text should be editable by the Owner and reviewed by a lawyer before real use.

Build:
1. Owner can create/edit Media Buyer Agreement template.
2. Media Buyer must accept the agreement before accessing dashboard.
3. Store accepted agreement snapshot.
4. Store acceptance date/time.
5. Store mediaBuyerId.
6. Store IP hash and userAgent hash if practical.
7. Store typed legal name.
8. Optional signature field.
9. Generate/download PDF copy if practical.
10. Owner can view acceptance status.

Agreement should cover:
- scope of marketing services
- commission rules
- paid orders only
- excluded orders: pending, failed, cancelled, refunded
- refund/chargeback commission reversal
- payout schedule
- ad spend responsibility
- tracking links and attribution
- dashboard/system as source of truth
- brand usage rules
- confidentiality
- data privacy
- no access to private student/parent data
- termination notice
- governing law/jurisdiction placeholder
- owner right to approve/reject commissions

Routes:
- /media/agreement
- /media/agreement/accept
- /owner/media-buyers/agreements
- /owner/media-buyers/[id]/agreement

Rules:
- Media Buyer cannot access /media/dashboard until agreement is accepted.
- Owner can update agreement template.
- If agreement changes materially, Owner can require re-acceptance.
- Accepted agreement snapshot must not change if template is edited later.
- Owner can download/view accepted agreement.

Database:
MediaBuyerAgreementTemplate:
- id
- title
- version
- content
- active
- requiresReacceptance
- createdAt
- updatedAt

MediaBuyerAgreementAcceptance:
- id
- mediaBuyerId
- templateId
- templateVersion
- acceptedContentSnapshot
- typedName
- signatureData optional
- ipHash
- userAgentHash
- acceptedAt

Acceptance criteria:
- Media Buyer sees agreement on first login.
- Media Buyer must accept before dashboard access.
- Owner can view accepted agreement.
- Agreement snapshot is preserved.
- Owner can require re-acceptance after template update.
